  "$comment": "languages-world-2 (11 November 2026): the WhatsApp allergen guard’s trigger words for AMHARIC (am-ET): አለርጂ / አለርጅ (inside ለአለርጂ, አለርጂክ), አይስማማኝም / የማይስማማ, ሴሊያክ, ያለ <allergen> (spaced and joined: ያለ ወተት / ያለወተት), ከ<allergen> ነጻ / ነፃ, <allergen> የሌለው / የለውም / አልያዘም, አትጨምሩ / ሳትጨምሩ, መብላት አልችልም, ደህንነቱ, ሊይዝ ይችላል, ቅሪት, ብክለት / የተበከለ, ላክቶስ — prefixes (ለ ከ የ በ) ride along. Ethiopic syllables carry no combining marks, so spellings are listed per variant letter (ነጻ / ነፃ, ዓሳ / አሳ, ደህንነቱ / ደኅንነቱ). Bare ያለ (ያለበት = where), bare ነፃ (free of charge), bare ደህና (a greeting) and bare ተስማሚ (ተስማሚ ዋጋ = fair price) are NOT stems, and ጾም (fasting food) is a religious choice, not a free-from safety word, and is left out. OPTION B, as every other language: absence / safety words only, NOT the bare allergen names (a presence question may reach the AI, which answers only from the tags and gets the caveat). Matched with the Unicode normaliser. caveatWords: a tagged label of the codex allergen set (stored in English, lower case) → the words a reply may use for it (matched on the raw lower-cased reply, so written as the AI writes them). The country has no allergen set of its own yet, so caveatWords are for 'codex' (as MX, SG, HK, MY, TH and AE).",
